  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICNL- Mapping and Typology of State Involvement in Civil Society Networks and Representative Bodies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strong independent networks and representative bodies are an important component of the infrastructure supporting civil society. They serve crucial functions, such as bringing civil society together to develop and advocate for common positions on issues of importance to the sector, building the governance and management capacities of member organizations, fostering collaboration, and sponsoring voluntary codes of conduct to help NGOs adhere to good governance standards, which in turn fosters trust for civil society among the public.</narrative>
  </description>
